A||N||7||bHooper||sunroof latch, doesnt stay open!||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||03-11-2001||09:36 AM||||hey guys, for years, i have been battleing my darned sunroof latch.  it doesnt always want to stay in the open position.  it pivots and does everything its supposed to, but just doesnt lock.<P>what can i do about this?  are these parts still available?<P>thanks!<P>hoop<P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||03-11-2001||07:53 PM||||Hoop,<P>My coupe did the same thing. When you push the latch back to hold the roof up, once it stops, wiggle the latch side to side just a bit, and it should go back another 1/2-3/4 inch. <BR>This worked for me. Your mileage may vary.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||03-11-2001||08:55 PM||||i'll give that a try, tomorrow.<P>thanks!<BR>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||03-11-2001||09:23 PM||||hoop, that latch is adjustable.........take the cover off (one phillips head screw) and you will see two nuts holding the latch mechanism to the room on two studs......the latch is adjustable from front to rear......try different positions to get the desired result but always remember to check it in the "closed" position too!||||reg||1
Z||000004||bHooper||03-11-2001||09:41 PM||||i'll give that a check now.||||reg||1
Z||000005||bHooper||03-11-2001||10:01 PM||||terry,<P>that seems to have worked!  it stays open fine now.<P>don't laugh... but i've been "dealing" with this little problem for 10 years!  the car was broken into, through the latch, 10 years ago.  and hasn't stayed open very consistantly ever since!<P>and having just done a half a$$ job of replacing the headliner, it has been worse.<P>thanks!<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000006||Standard||03-12-2001||12:36 AM||||Mine rattles a bit, but it usually stays open.  Sometimes when I go over a big bump it slams shut and scares the beejeezus out of me...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  Took me awhile to figure out what it was the first time it happened..  I'll get around to adjusting it sometime...||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||03-12-2001||01:29 AM||||great hoop, glad I could help........by the way, we are doing headliners with the fiberglass board........we can either supply the materials or the completed headliner (if you are ever in need of the other half of that half a$$ job!)(just kidding........)<P>I couldn't get my sunroof glass to seat right after I replaced the gasket so I took the latch apart and added another of the plastic spacers.........now it locks down tight and seats well in the gasket -- now there are no leaks when it rains hard!!||||reg||1
